# PayCraft dashboard → Cloudflare PAGES project RUNTIME secret map
# (`wrangler pages secret put <ENV> --project-name paycraft`).
# (Authoritative alias→env-NAME mapping — replaces the guessy sync, since the
#  dashboard reads env names that differ from the vault env_var fields, and some
#  values are needed under TWO names. Consumed by infra/deploy/deploy.sh
#  phase_2_secrets_sync at `/paycraft-deploy prod`.)
#
# Format:  ENV_NAME = vault-alias
#          ENV_NAME = vault-alias | optional: <why the dashboard works without it>
#   - Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#   - The SAME vault-alias may back MULTIPLE env names (value set under each).
#   - Every entry is REQUIRED unless marked optional WITH a reason. A required alias
#     that does not resolve, or any failed write, FAILS deploy phase 2 (it used to
#     warn and report PASS). See infra/deploy/lib-secrets-sync.sh.
#
# Provenance (2026-08-23): the 15 core secrets already exist in the mbs vault
# with real values. Vercel could NOT be the migration source — its prod env vars
# are type "Sensitive" (write-only; `vercel env pull` returns "[SENSITIVE]"). The
# vault is the SoT. NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV + NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYCRAFT_DASHBOARD_URL are
# NON-secret → set in wrangler.jsonc `vars`, not here.
#
# Deliberately OMITTED:
#   POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN   — lib/email.ts is dead code (imported nowhere); never loads.
#   STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID     — code has a safe fallback ("price_pro_monthly").
#   STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_PRICE_ID — code fallback ("price_enterprise_monthly").
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID       — public GA id; optional; set as a var if analytics wanted.

# ── Supabase ──
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL          = framework-supabase-url
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYCRAFT_SUPABASE_URL = framework-supabase-url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY     = framework-supabase-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY         = framework-supabase-service-role-key

# ── Stripe (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY + the PAYCRAFT_CLOUD_* alias share one value) ──
# Org-tier alias per RULE-SECRETS-NAMING-CONVENTION-001. The old `paycraft-stripe-platform-secret-key`
# was never registered, and the pre-2026-11-07 phase 2 skipped unresolvable aliases silently, so these
# two were never actually synced by a deploy.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY                 = mbs-stripe-platform-secret-key
PAYCRAFT_CLOUD_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY  = mbs-stripe-platform-secret-key
STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID          = paycraft-stripe-connect-client-id | optional: lib/stripe-client.ts reads the client id from the DB first and handles null

# ── OAuth state signing (reuses the encryption key per project decision) ──
PAYCRAFT_OAUTH_STATE_SECRET       = paycraft-encryption-key
